--   Exact helper polynomials for first-recurrence inner5
-- statement:
--   These are the exact original pure helper polynomials used by six original first-recurrence inner5 arithmetic lemmas. Every newly exported value is independently compared with the pinned original using kernel-checked reflexivity. No equality certificate, nonvanishing assertion or theorem proof is assumed. The named downstream consumers are the original B6-square, left-product, shift-product, quotient-product, exceptional-product and residual identities, followed by the exact normalized inner5 certificate and full every-curve order49 exclusion.
-- source:
--   User MazurTheorem WIP54d43d8dda8a6fcf069cc02a815f850d762c5c0c, Apache-2.0 headers and attribution preserved. Exact original kernel type dependencies of the six original helper lemmas select these pure definitions. Complete original Lean AST declarations and resolved reference ranges preserve every value; private visibility changes only at exact private-token ranges. Every value is independently kernel-compared to its actual original constant name, including private constants. The published normalized coefficient data are reused. This package carries no constructed proof and cannot discharge a child lemma by itself.

